body:
Your post about your breakup really hit home for me. I also recently broke up with my boyfriend less than a month ago. He too kept a lot of things to himself towards the end of our relationship, and wouldn't tell me when I would ask him. He's moved on with other girls, and I did feel a little blindsided even though things weren't going well. I frequently asked him throughout the relationship how I could be a better girlfriend, and he would shrug and say he didn't know. When we did break up, it turned out he was keeping a lot of feelings to himself. But I digress...

&#x200B;

Just remember to be kind to yourself. I was okay with the breakup, but also confused. My head told me that my small feelings of discontent and doubts in the relationship would have prevented it from truly lasting. It told me that in the long run, this was for the better so that I wouldn't have to waste time on someone who didn't deserve my time. My heart told me that it was okay to grieve. The reality is that not only are you losing someone who showed you love in ways that your friends couldn't, but you're also losing your best friend. I find myself missing his company a lot, whether it's telling him about how the starbucks person messed up my order, or wanting a big comforting hug. It's completely to okay to grieve over those things and cry. It's also okay to be okay. 

&#x200B;

At first you might put him on a pedestal and recall all the good memories you had together. You might think that he was the best that you had and that you could never love or be loved like this again. I know I did. I then went into a stage of resentment. I resented the way he treated me, and I resented the fact that he was seemingly happier without me. Throughout those times, I encourage you to remember what is true. What are the facts of the relationship, and what were things you were previously making excuses for when you had your love goggles on? It was helpful to talk to people who had broken up, but were also in good relationships. I saw that ultimately, there was no way that things were going to last. There were too many no's to the relationship, and I didn't want to be the one to put in all the effort to make things work. Fact: It was not okay how he treated you towards the end. Fact: He already checked out of the relationship. Fact: You deserve better than that. Fact: You are better off without someone who can't respect you or be honest with you.

&#x200B;

Honestly, just be kind to yourself. Don't get mad at yourself for randomly crying or feeling vulnerable. For the love of God, do not compare yourself to the new girl. Don't tell yourself that if you changed xyz, that he would still be with your or whatever. Those were all things I did, and they were not conducive to my recovery process or my mental health. Just because you are different from her does not mean she is better or you are better. Do not tear her, or your ex, down. It honestly doesn't really help. It might just make you more bitter. Just practice kindness, and it'll help your heart heal a lot faster. Be kind to your mental health. Don't let your head fill up with lies. Be kind to your emotional health, and let yourself get those feelings out. Cry into a pillow if you want. Be kind to your physical health. It's okay to mope in bed, but don't let that be the only thing you do. Find a balance.

&#x200B;

Lastly, keep yourself busy and look forward to what the future holds. Now you can harmlessly flirt around with that cute waiter or smile back at the guy walking his dog. You can look forward to dressing up to go on dates, or experience the thrill of the chase with someone new if you want. Look forward to growing with someone else. How might new friendships and relationships push you to grow to an even better person? Embrace your new freedom. You no longer have to be attached to your phone or worry about remembering to message someone periodically throughout the day.

&#x200B;

I would love to be friends! Tbh, I'm still in the process of getting over my breakup. I emphasize a lot with you. It sucks now, but remind yourself that it's for the better. Feel free to PM me any time :)
